{
  "reason": "The evolution shows the meta-stacking paradigm is the bottleneck: adding more base learners (DeepFM/LR then XGB/CB) monotonically regressed (0.7645 -> 0.7635 vs the earlier 0.7670), meaning the stack is fitting OOF noise rather than adding signal on ~8k low-cardinality rows. Root cause is twofold: (1) a learned meta-learner plus best-of-five OOF selection overfits the tiny OOF vector, and (2) heavy hand-crafted categorical interaction features plus many candidates inflate variance. The fix is a Tier 2 representation/ensemble change: a simpler, more regularized ensemble with a fixed robust blend (no learned meta, no best-of-N selection) and a threshold tuned per fold and averaged, which trades a little bias for much lower variance on held-out data.",
  "module": ["model_design", "training_evaluation"],
  "plan": {
    "model_design": "WHAT: Replace the 'many weak learners + learned meta-LGBM with best-of-five selection' scheme with a small, deliberately decorrelated two-family ensemble: (a) CatBoost on RAW categorical strings passed via cat_features (letting ordered target statistics model coupon x feature conditionals without hand-crafted interaction columns), and (b) the existing LightGBM on the engineered categorical frame. Keep factories make_catboost/make_lightgbm but tune CatBoost depth=6, l2_leaf_reg=5, iterations raised only if time budget allows; drop XGBoost from the production blend (it was the most redundant with LGBM). WHY: on this 8k-row, 21-nominal dataset the marginal value is in regularization and diversity between ordered-target-stat and histogram splits, not in stacking depth; removing XGB and the learned meta cuts variance that caused the regressions. HOW: preserve signatures _train_catboost/_predict_catboost (add raw-string variants that consume fe_df columns directly) and _train_lgbm/_predict_lgbm; keep bundle keys lgb_models, cb_models, cat_maps, cat_cols, num_cols, scaler, label_map, threshold; set use_stack=False and remove reliance on meta_model in predict.",
    "training_evaluation": "WHAT: Replace the learned-meta + best-of-{lgb_avg,xgb_avg,cb_avg,soft_vote,meta_gbdt} OOF selection with a fixed soft-probability blend of {LGBM, CatBoost} (simple mean of rank-normalized or raw probabilities) and a per-fold threshold tuning that averages thresholds across folds instead of one global threshold. WHY: selecting the argmax candidate on the OOF vector overfits; a pre-committed equal-weight blend is metric-faithful (accuracy via a threshold) and lower-variance, and averaging per-fold thresholds reduces threshold-overfit to the training distribution. HOW: in the 5-fold train-only CV, still fit CouponFeatureEngineer/_fit_cat_maps/StandardScaler per fold on TRAIN rows only; for each fold compute LGBM and CatBoost val probabilities, build blend=mean, call _tune_threshold per fold, collect thresholds; then set the persisted threshold = median of per-fold thresholds and report the blend accuracy using the fold-averaged threshold as the OOF score (still accuracy_score-based, matching the official metric). Persist use_stack=False, selected='blend', and skip meta_model fitting. Preserve _tune_threshold, make_stratified_folds, the argparse train/predict signatures, row_id 0..N-1 output with original labels via inv_map, and fresh-process reload semantics (predict must reload bundle.joblib and never refit); keep 3-seed bagging for each family only if total train time stays under 600s."
  }
}
